<title>UK: SOCCER-EUROPEAN CUP WINNERS' CUP FIRST ROUND SECOND LEG RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-EUROPEAN CUP WINNERS' CUP FIRST ROUND SECOND LEG RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of European Cup Winners'</p>
<p>Cup first round, second leg soccer matches on Thursday:</p>
<p>Nyva Vinnytsya (Ukraine) 0 Sion (Switzerland) 4 (halftime</p>
<p>0-2)</p>
<p>Scorers: Vladan Lukic (3rd), Philippe Vercruyse (9th, 66th),</p>
<p>Milton De Suza (54th).</p>
<p>Sion wins 6-0 on aggregate</p>
<p>Attendance 15,000</p>
<p>In Varazdin: Varteks Varazdin (Croatia) 2 Lokomotiv Moscow</p>
<p>(Russia) 1 (0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Varazdin - Davor Vugrinec, 63rd, 79th</p>
<p>Lokomotiv - Kosolapov, 40th</p>
<p>Aggregate score 2-2. Lokomotiv win on away goal rule.</p>
<p>Ruch Chorzow (Poland) 0 Benfica (Portugal) 0</p>
<p>Attendance: 4,547</p>
<p>Benfica win 5-1 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Humenne: Chemlon Humenne (Slovakia) 1 AEK Athens (Greece)</p>
<p>2 (1-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Chemlon Humenne - Pavol Dina (1st minute)</p>
<p>AEK - Demis Nikolaidis (19th), Daniel Batista Lima (44th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 14,700</p>
<p>AEK win 3-1 on agregate</p>
<p>In Istanbul: Galatasaray (Turkey) 4 Constructorul Chisinau</p>
<p>(Moldova) 0 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Hakan Sukur (49th, 80th mins), Arif Erdem (73rd),</p>
<p>George Hagi (75th)</p>
<p>Attendance 20,000</p>
<p>Galatasaray win 5-0 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Solna: AIK Solna (Sweden) 1 Reykjavik (Iceland) 1 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>AIK - Pascal Simpson (79th)</p>
<p>Reykjavik - Gudmundur Benediktsson (90th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 3,267.</p>
<p>AIK win 2-1 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Prague: Sparta Prague (Czech Republic) 1  Sturm Graz</p>
<p>(Austria ) 1 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Sparta - Michal Hornak (85th minute)</p>
<p>Sturm - Ivica Vastic (76th)</p>
<p>Aggregate score 3-3, Spart Prague win on away goals rule</p>
<p>In Bergen: Brann (Norway) 4 Cercle Brugge (Belgium) 0  </p>
<p>(1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Mons Ivar Mjelde (5th), Claus Eftevaag (79th),</p>
<p>Mjelde (82nd), Roger Helland (88th).</p>
<p>Attendance: 6,104</p>
<p>Brann win on 6-3 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Eindhoven: PSV Eindhoven (Netherlands) 3 Dynamo Batumi</p>
<p>(Georgia) 0 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Luc Nilis (15th, penalty), Rene Eykelkamp (53rd),</p>
<p>Marcelo (83rd)</p>
<p>Attendance: 14,200</p>
<p>PSV win 4-1 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Florence: Fiorentina (Italy) 1 Gloria Bistrita (Romania)</p>
<p>0 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Massimo Orlando (22nd)</p>
<p>Attendance: 20,000</p>
<p>Fiorentina win 2-1 on agregate</p>
<p>In Budapest: Kispest Honved (Hungary) 1 Nimes (France) 2</p>
<p>(0-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Kispest Honved - Attila Piroska (61st)</p>
<p>Nimes - Johnny Ecker (7th), Eric Sabin (38th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 6,000</p>
<p>Nimes win 5-2 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Larnaca: AEK Larnaca (Cyprus) 0  Barcelona (Spain) 0</p>
<p>Attendance: 6,000</p>
<p>Barcelona win 2-0 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Paris: Paris Saint-Germain (France) 3 Vaduz</p>
<p>(Liechtenstein) 0 (2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Bernard Allou (22nd), Alain Roche (40th), Patrick</p>
<p>Mboma (48th)</p>
<p>PSG win 7-0 on aggregate</p>
<p>Attendance: 15,973</p>
<p>In Liverpool: Liverpool (England) 3 MyPa-47 (Finland) 1</p>
<p>(1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Liverpool - Patrick Berger (18th), Stan Collymore (59th),</p>
<p>John Barnes (78th)</p>
<p>MyPa-47 - Mauri Keskitalo (64th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 39,013</p>
<p>Liverpool win 4-1 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Belgrade: Red Star Belgrade (Yugoslavia) 4 Kaiserlautern</p>
<p>(Germany) 0. (after extra time. 90 mins 1-0).</p>
<p>Scorers: Dejan Stankovic (55th, 97th) Njegus (107th),</p>
<p>Pantelic (120th).</p>
<p>Attendance: 70,000</p>
<p>Red Star win 4-1 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Ljubljana: Olimpija Ljubljana (Slovenia) 0 Aarhus</p>
<p>(Demnark) 0. Aggregate 1-1. Olimpija win on away goals rule</p>
